    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0636" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg538"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cridler to Mr.
                            Hollis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copies of two letters<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d650-f1"/> from Messrs. Hopkins &amp; Hopkins, complaining of
                    the action of the British Government in seizing, off Delagoa Bay, the steamships
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Mashona</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Maria</hi>,
                    both of which carried goods shipped by Messrs. Flint, Eddy &amp; Co., of New
                    York. You will please investigate the matter and report thereon to the
                    Department. You will also use all proper efforts to protect the property of the
                    American shippers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. W. Cridler</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Third Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d650-f1" n="2" xml:id="d650-f1-content">
                <p>(Inclosures:) From Hopkins &amp; Hopkins, December 12, 1899, and December 15,
                    1899, printed ante.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
